From f3cb785ef279ccd2744622588bdb8cf6a40875e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:05:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add an admin API for the users' blocking lists (XEP-0191)

The blocking lists of mod_blocking can be changed only by the user's
own session, with the blocking command. Services that manage blocks on
behalf of their users have to keep a session open for each user.

Add a 'blocking' admin GraphQL category (and the matching mongooseimctl
commands) with getBlockingList, block and unblock. The changes have the
same effect as the blocking command: the list is stored as the default
privacy list, the user's online resources get the blocking push, and
the presences of the affected contacts are updated. Domain admins can
manage the lists of the users in their domain.

mod_blocking gets get_blocking_list/3 and set_blocking_list/5 for that,
reused by the IQ handlers. A failed write of the privacy list now
returns an internal-server-error instead of crashing the IQ handler.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ETaRHXo1LmPHqZB9SXMucM
